e12dca90ae58fec3c9765095/MPN/FFT/Product.lean#L1176-L1179"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./MPN/FFT/Product.html#MPN.FFT.FFTOps.fftParams\"><span class=\"name\">MPN</span>.<span class=\"name\">FFT</span>.<span class=\"name\">FFTOps</span>.<span class=\"name\">fftParams</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">w </span><span class=\"fn\">T </span><span class=\"fn\">k</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Prod\">×</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The parameters for `T` limbs and `K = 2ᵏ` pieces of `w`-bit limbs: pieces of\n`m = ⌈T / (K - 1)⌉` limbs, so that the two operands have at most `K + 1`, and residues of `n`\nlimbs, `2 m + 1` rounded up to a multiple of `K / (2 w)`, so that the root `2^(2 w n / K)` is a\npower of two.","docLink":"./MPN/FFT/Product.html#MPN.FFT.FFTOps.fftParams","kind":"def","line":1165,"name":"MPN.FFT.FFTOps.fftParams","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-mpn/blob/0c3e72656c98060de12dca90ae58fec3c9765095/MPN/FFT/Product.lean#L1165-L1174"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./MPN/FFT/Product.html#MPN.FFT.FFTOps.fftSqrAt_spec\"><span class=\"name\">MPN</span>.<span class=\"name\">FFT</span>.<span class=\"name\">FFTOps</span>.<span class=\"name\">fftSqrAt_spec</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">A </span><span class=\"fn\">L</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">[<span class=\"fn\">LA</span> : <span class=\"f